<div class="page">
  <div class="sub-heading">There are 12 points in 1 pica.</div>
  <ul class="instruction-list">
    <li>A point is a unit of a measurement that is the standard for typesetting and publication design is picas.</li>
    <li>A measuring depth of printing. One point is equal to .013836 of an inch and 72 points are approximately 1 inch.</li>
    <li>A pica is a typesetting unit of measurement commonly used for measuring lines of type.</li>
    <li>One pica equals 12 points. There are 6 picas to an inch.</li>
    <li>A standard US letter size page is 8.5 by 11 inches or 51 by 66 picas. (6 picas = 12 pts, plus the leftover)</li>
    <li>The letter p is used to designate picas as in 22p or 6p. With 12 points to the pica, half a pica would be 6 points written as 06p. 17 points would be 1p5 (1 pica = 12 pts, plus the leftover)</li>
  </ul>
</div>

